# tools/local/ — rigs that drive the RUNNING product rather than its sources: the XTest window
# driver, the channel stomper, the state seeder and the geometry probe. See tools/local/README.md
# for what each one measures.
#
# Untracked as a category, not for being unfinished. Each needs something a phase gate may never
# depend on — a live X server, libXtst, a running JACK server, a built bundle, a directory of
# captures — and a gate that needs a window server is a gate that cannot run. The tracked gate on
# the same code is tools/panelrender.cpp, which renders every page offline and audits the art.
tools/local/

# Renders written by the offline audit tools into whatever directory they are run from.
#
# panelrender and rackrender take an output PREFIX as their first argument and default to writing
# beside the working directory, so running either from the top of the tree drops a dozen PNGs into
# it. They are build output in the same sense an object file is: regenerated by the gate on every
# run, different after any layout change, and reviewed by looking at them rather than by diffing
# them. Eleven of them were tracked for a while and every UI change then showed up as a binary diff
# nobody could read.
#
# Anchored to the top level, so the real art under resources/ and gui/ is untouched.
/*.png
